**Exemplary Patent Claim Language**

1. A spinal implant comprising:  
   a first transverse plate member and a second transverse plate member;  
   a plurality of longitudinally extending arcuate portions associated with the first and second transverse plate members, the arcuate portions having complementary mating configurations configured to interengage the first and second transverse plate members;  
   a central through-channel extending through the implant and configured to receive bone-graft material; and  
   an articulation mechanism permitting relative biaxial movement between the first and second transverse plate members about first and second axes, thereby enabling adjustment of the implant to correct a spinal deformity.
